################################################################################
# RECONCILIATION AGAINST THE LOCK — where reproduction diverged from testimony
################################################################################

The lock is testimony. Every number above was re-derived from the source tree in
this session. Four divergences are recorded rather than silently adopted:

1. LINE NUMBERS HAVE DRIFTED. The lock cites e.g. Skills.module.css:187 for
   `padding: 0.6rem clamp(...)`; at HEAD d1fce27 that declaration is at
   Skills.module.css:176. Two commits landed after the lock was written
   (f642b41 "let the chart be read against the years it is drawn to",
   e480687 "the bench on a phone is a filter, not a second list"). Every
   file:line in this log is from HEAD, not from the lock.

2. COUNT. The lock states "107 declarations carrying 113 non-conforming values
   - 35 4pt half-steps, 72 off-grid, plus 3 hairline exemptions" (35+72=107,
   not 113). An independent scan at HEAD finds 110 non-conforming values
   (73 off-grid + 37 half-step) plus the same 3 hairline exemptions. The lock's
   finding reproduces; its arithmetic does not add up and its totals are three
   values light.

3. FALSE POSITIVE — "3 animation sites under 200 ms". Only ONE site is under
   the interface floor at runtime: Listen.module.css:118,
   `transition: transform 120ms var(--motion-ease-standard)`. The other two the
   lock names, Bench.module.css:165-166 (now :165-166 -> :164-165 in the
   multi-line declaration at :163), are `var(--motion-fast, 180ms)` — the 180ms
   is a var() FALLBACK. `--motion-fast` is always defined (globals.css:86), so
   the computed duration at those two sites is 220ms, inside the band. The
   Playwright run confirms it: at all four breakpoints exactly two rendered
   durations are out of band, and neither is a Bench wire. The 180ms literals
   are still reported by TC-NFR-MOTION-TOKENISED as untokenised dead fallbacks —
   which is what they actually are — not as band violations.

4. UNDER-REPORT — "Compositor-safe properties: PRESENT ... No width/height/
   top/left animation." Not true at HEAD. Experience.module.css:159 transitions
   `height` and `top` on `.trackBar` (the timeline bar grows and shifts on hover
   and when active, :164-168). Both are layout-triggering. This is a genuine
   R-46 violation the lock missed, and TC-NFR-MOTION-COMPOSITOR fails on it.
   `stroke-width` (Bench.module.css:47) is NOT counted: an SVG paint property
   repaints the shape without reflowing the document, the same cost class as
   the `stroke-opacity` the lock itself endorses.

Additionally, the lock's motion audit was scoped to the eleven section/mark
modules. app/globals.css was scanned here too, because R-46 governs interface
motion and not merely section motion, and it carries the larger share of the
violations: 0.5s (nav-link), 0.08s and 1.4s durations, plus nine timing
keywords and two omitted timing functions.

